  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The starting material is an equiatomic, as-cast CoCrFeNi high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at.% Al and applying a low-temperature surface activation treatment will produce an in situ continuous alumina glaze during sliding.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::030::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC10241162::web::036::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed alumina glaze will be self-healing.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A brief exposure at 100–200 °C in a controlled atmosphere can activate the surface for immediate oxide-layer formation.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperatures, Al in the modified CoCrFeNi alloy will rapidly oxidize to form stable, adherent alumina.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::030::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC10241162::web::036::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "A dense protective oxide glaze can minimize oxidative and adhesive wear during high-temperature sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::030::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC10241162::web::036::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alumina nanoparticles can form within a high-temperature tribochemical glaze or deformed tribolayer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::030::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC10241162::web::036::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, the activation treatment will ensure that a thin, continuous protective oxide is already present.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The room-temperature oxide will reduce metal-to-metal contact and friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The protective oxide layer will remain continuous and durable from 25 °C to 800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified, pre-activated alloy will have lower friction coefficients than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified, pre-activated alloy will have lower wear rates than unmodified CoCrFeNi throughout 25–800 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::030::adaptive_friction_interface_protection",
        "PMC10241162::web::036::adaptive_friction_interface_protection"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi lacks a protective oxide film under the proposed sliding conditions.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Unmodified CoCrFeNi experiences higher friction and accelerated wear, particularly when oxidation and adhesive wear become prominent at elevated temperature.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intended test range is 25–800 °C under an approximately 50 N normal load.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intended environment is ambient or controlled atmosphere with moderate humidity.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The efficacy of the low-temperature activation treatment in producing continuous alumina at room temperature is uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The long-term stability of the oxide during cyclic or prolonged high-temperature sliding is uncertain.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
